artbeat: the controller follows `pods/log` into the host log; log mtime.","-   - Logs: followed into `~/.ard/logs/...`; stdout from the tee file shipped in the result.","-4. **New paragraph \"Kubernetes-executor details\"** right after the table, same style as \"Local-executor details\". Cover: the flow; decisions 1-8 and 10-12 (volume, push result, pod shape and key isolation, key lifecycle, exit code from the kubelet and `Gone` never `Exited` 0, untar rules, listener, logs and heartbeat, cluster, REST client without client-go, images); the pod paths `/job`, `/work`, `/role`, `/sidecar`, `/ard-config`, `/ard-out`, `/ard-bin`; the result layout (input roots `work/ role/ config/ sidecar/`, result roots `work/ out/`, stdout at `out/stdout` outside `work/`; gap 2); the deadline arithmetic (gap 13: `h.Deadline = Start + Timeout`, job-exec deadline `h.Deadline - min(2m, Timeout/10)`, pod `activeDeadlineSeconds = Timeout + UploadGrace` (2 min), key revoked at `Deadline + UploadGrace`, job-exec exits 124 which maps to `TimedOut`); the exit code stored in `<id>.done` at accept (gap 14); upload grace for the `upload` container; pod name limit (`ard-<id>` at most 63, ids over 59 rejected, lowercased ids; gap 12); `job-exec` reaps orphans as PID 1 (gap 18); handles of the other executor kind report `Gone` (gap 15); orphan-pod sweep scoped by an `ard/repo` hash label (gap 16); default input size limits agreeing with the `emptyDir` `sizeLimit` (gap 19, name the defaults as \"from the tarball limits plus the job resources flags\"); the executor is not an effect. State the owner's answers: TLS option A (self-signed ECDSA P-256 cert generated in memory at `ard serve` start, SAN the Service DNS name, SHA-256 of the leaf pinned in each per-job Secret as `fingerprint`, verified with `VerifyConnection`; restart rotates it); `--job-api-tls=self-signed|off`, `off` only under dry-run (mark this flag as planned for part 4); cluster settings (jobs namespace, API address, images) are `ard se