es not mount; role dir from `cfg.SHA`, so k8s refuses a config without a SHA; sidecars at pinned SHAs; untrusted inputs and scrub list in the per-job Secret, capped at 768 KiB, over the cap a permanent failure with a named cause; copies the static `ard` binary); `agent` (mounts only `work` and `out`, holds only its model credential via `secretKeyRef`, no GitHub token, key, Secret volume or SA token; tees stdout to `out/stdout`, enforces its deadline, writes a done marker, reaps orphans as PID 1); `post` (own pinned image, never runs a binary from a shared volume; one route `GET /v1/result` on the pod IP, preshared 32-byte `crypto/rand` key unique to the pod, mounted only in `post`, kept in memory by the controller, constant-time compare; 409 until the agent has terminated and the marker exists; builds the tar in Go, never runs git; one concurrent request; header/idle timeouts; never logs Authorization; exits 0 after the controller confirms or the deadline). Plain HTTP inside the cluster, because the key grants only this job's result and NetworkPolicy limits who can connect.","+   - Controller: `Prepare` builds the local workspace; mints the read token, key and per-job Secret (owned by the Pod); revokes the token (`DELETE /installation/token`) after `pre` terminates; tokens join the redaction set. Completion is decided only from the kubelet (`containerStatuses`, agent `state.terminated`), never from the agent-writable done marker; the controller then pulls the result and safe-untars into `<id>.result` (rules: `os.Root`, regular files/dirs/symlinks with symlinks last, modes masked to 0644/0755, reject hardlinks, devices, FIFOs, `..`, absolute paths, NUL, duplicates, any `.git` component, case-fold collisions; caps on compressed and decompressed bytes counted on the stream, entry count, per-file size, gzip ratio). Close-out runs unchanged (`gitx.Snapshot` against `BaseSHA`). Exit code comes from the kubelet only and is saved in `<id>.done` (gap 14); a pod that ends with no valid result is `Gone`, never `Exited` 0. Statuses: `Running`, `Orphaned`, `Exited`, `TimedOut`, `Gone`. Requires GitHub App auth (a PAT cannot be scoped down). Keys are not persisted: after a restart the Reaper kills orphan pods, and a sweep by an `ard/repo` hash label finds pods with no state record (gap 16). Handles of the other executor kind report `Gone` (gap 15). Pod and job names: lowercased id, `ard-<id>` at most 63 so ids over 59 are rejected (gap 12). Client: thin REST client over the in-cluster SA token behind an interface with a fake, no client-go.","+   - Layout and limits: pod paths `/job`, `/work`, `/role`, `/sidecar`, `/ard-config`, `/ard-out`, `/ard-bin`; result roots `work/` and `out/` (stdout at `out/stdout`, outside `work/`, so it never shows in `Snapshot.Changed`; gap 2). Defaults: 2 GiB `emptyDir` per pod, result 512 MiB compressed and 2 GiB unpacked, 200k files, 100 MiB per file, all overridable by `ard serve` flags (gap 19).","+   - Deadlines (gap 13): `h.Deadline = Start + Timeout`; job-exec deadline `h.Deadline - min(2m, Timeout/10)`; pod `activeDeadlineSeconds = Timeout + UploadGrace` (2 min; name it as the result-pull grace); key revoked at `Deadline + grace`; job-exec exits 124 at its deadline, which maps to `TimedOut`.","+   - Settings and images: cluster settings (jobs namespace, images, sizes) are `ard serve` flags set by the chart, not `.ard/config.yaml`; `executor` is fixed at startup and a later config with a different value is a config error until restart (gap 6). The `ard-agent` image is public under `ghcr.io/albertcbrown/ard`, holds no secrets (an image test checks it), and carries Go, jq, yq, osv-scanner, govulncheck and golangci-lint at the repo's pins but not trufflehog (AGPL); roles with a `Dockerfile` use it until in-cluster builds exist (gap 7). The executor is not an effect (dry-run runs it as local jobs run today). State that the work is split across later parts, and that #317 splits into the API layer and the executor."," 5. **Job TTL sentence.** Replace \"the Kubernetes `Job` gets a short TTL\" with: a Kubernetes job's pod and per-job Secret are deleted (no Job object, no TTL).","-6. **Configuration section.** (a) Dockerfile bullet: under `executor: k8s` every role runs the default `ard-agent` image and a role `Dockerfile` is ignored until in-cluster builds exist (own issue); name the affected starter roles, i.e. the scanners `cve`, `docs`, `error-codes`, `lint`, `missing-tests`, `trufflehog` (`internal/roles/scanners/*/Dockerfile`) and any worker whose tests need a toolchain, and say the rollout must either put their tools in the public image or keep them off under k8s (gap 7). (b) Config yaml: `executor: local # local | k8s; fixed at startup`; add one sentence after the block saying cluster settings are `ard serve` flags set by the chart.","-7. **Guardrails.** Replace the egress clause \"in Kubernetes a network policy limits egress to the model API and package registries\" with: in Kubernetes job egress is DNS, the job API and the internet minus private ranges and 169.254.169.254 (matching the #276 posture). Add four bullets after that bullet: **Job API key** (decision 4), **Job API listener** (decision 7 plus TLS option A), **Result untar is the boundary** (decision 6), **Cluster** (decision 10). The Cluster bullet lists the residual risks: the model credential sits in a per-job Secret in etcd, so it relies on etcd encryption at rest (gap 17); the tee'd stdout is agent-writable, so the agent can forge its own usage figures, the same exposure local Docker has today, accepted by the owner, exit code still from the kubelet, revisit when split log streams are available (gap 1); pod egress reaches the whole internet; Pod Security `restricted` relies on the cluster's admission. Drop the \"key added to the redaction set by value\" requirement from the text of decision 4 or mark it not planned (gap 5), and say so in the Open questions entry.","-8. **Open questions.** Append `- [x] **Kubernetes executor (#54).**` with a one-paragraph decided summary linking #54, the design comment and #312, plus the owner's answers. Add one unchecked `- [ ]` entry for each gap the owner has not settled: gap 5 (redaction of the key), gap 3 now moot under the plain upload container (record the grace period instead), gap 11 (worktree registration after the swap: prune versus export tree), gap 15/16 only if the details paragraph does not already decide them. Gaps 1, 4, 6, 13 and the owner's five answers are recorded as decided.","-9. No change to `docs/layout.md`. The Delivery \"Agent image\" bullet says the image \"is never published\". Leave that sentence for #320 (the owner assigned the change there), but add to the details paragraph that the k8s agent image will be public, so the two are not read as a contradiction; the worker notes the pending conflict in its PR.","+6. **Configuration section.** (a) Dockerfile bullet (currently says the k8s executor \"uses the default `ard-agent` image\"): under `executor: k8s` every role runs the default image and a role `Dockerfile` is ignored until in-cluster builds exist; the starter scanners `cve`, `docs`, `error-codes`, `lint`, `missing-tests` use the tools in the public image; `trufflehog` roles stay off under k8s and `ard config check` warns (planned, later part). (b) Config yaml line: `executor: local # local | k8s; fixed at startup`; add one sentence after the block that cluster settings are `ard serve` flags set by the chart.","+7. **Guardrails.** In \"Agents hold no GitHub token\", replace \"in Kubernetes a network policy limits egress to the model API and package registries\" with: in Kubernetes job egress is DNS and the internet minus private ranges and 169.254.169.254 (the #276 posture), and `pre` holds only a read-only per-job token revoked after it ends. Add bullets after it:","+   - **Isolated agent pod**: agent container holds only its model credential; `pre`/`post` run as a different UID; ValidatingAdmissionPolicy enforces `shareProcessNamespace: false` and refuses the App Secret, hostPath, a Secret mount in the agent container and an agent `runAsUser` equal to the sidecars'.","+   - **Result key and listener**: the `post` rules from step 4, plain HTTP and why; ingress to job pods only from the ard-serve pod on the post port; `ard serve` has no listener or Service for this.","+   - **Result untar is the boundary**: the rules from step 4.","+   - **Cluster**: jobs namespace with Pod Security `restricted`, job SA with no roles and no token, `enableServiceLinks: false`, non-root, drop ALL, RuntimeDefault seccomp, read-only root fs, `/tmp` on emptyDir, `restartPolicy: Never`, image pinned by digest; controller Role (namespaced): pods create/get/list/watch/delete, pods/log get, secrets create/delete, events list, no pods/exec. Residual risks: the model credential sits in a per-job Secret in etcd (require etcd encryption at rest); the tee'd stdout is agent-writable, so the agent can forge its usage figures, the same exposure as local Docker, accepted by the owner, exit code still from the kubelet, revisit when split log streams are available (gap 1); pod egress reaches the whole internet and a `network: false` pod still allows GitHub and model API CIDRs; Pod Security `restricted` relies on the cluster's admission.","+8. **Where it runs / Delivery.** The Delivery \"Agent image\" bullet says the image \"is never published\": leave that sentence (#320 changes it), but the details paragraph says the k8s image will be public so the two do not read as a contradiction; the worker notes the pending conflict in its PR.","+9. **Open questions.** Append `- [x] **Kubernetes executor (#54).**` with a short decided summary (revision 3, the owner's answers: no job API, post-container pull with a per-pod key, plain HTTP, tee-file stdout as accepted risk, public image, flags not config, `flock` on `ReadWriteOncePod`, size defaults, trufflehog off) linking #54, the design comment and #312